"""Owns this service's error taxonomy and the table that maps a category onto
a transport's way of reporting it.

Belongs here: the exception hierarchy for the six categories — invalid,
not_found, conflict, unauthorized, forbidden, internal — the helpers that wrap
a cause into one, and the category-to-status table.

Does NOT belong here: response bodies. The transport renders the RFC 9457
problem+json document; this package tells it which category it is holding. A
second transport adds a column to the table rather than a fork of it.

Driver exceptions and tracebacks never cross the transport boundary. Log the
detail, return the category.

Empty until Mint chunk 05.
"""
